## EXPERIMENTAL SECTIONS
Chemicals and Materials. Aminated-magnetic polystyrene microspheres ( $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -PSC) were supplied by Tianjin BaseLine ChromTech Research Centre (Tianjin,
China). Hydrogen tetrachloroaurate $\mathrm{(HAuCl_{4}{\cdot}4H_{2}O}$ , $99.9\%$ ), mercaptohexanol (MCH) and sodium ascorbate (AA) were purchased from Sigma Chemical Co. (St. Louis, MO). Tris-(2-carboxyethyl)-phosphine hydrochloride (TCEP) and DNA oligonucleotides were provided by Sangon Biotech Co., Ltd. (Shanghai, China). The corresponding sequences are listed in Table S1.
Apparatus. Electrochemical impedance spectroscopy (EIS), cyclic voltammetry (CV) and square wave voltammetry (SWV) were performed on a CHI 660D electrochemistry workstation (Shanghai Chenhua Instrument Co., Ltd., China) with a conventional three-electrode system.31 Polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis (PAGE) was recorded on a Bio-Rad imaging system (Hercules, CA, U.S.A.).
Preparation of 3D DNA walking machine modified on PSC. Modification of aminated PSC with 3D DNA walking machine was synthesized by Au-N coupling. Firstly, ${500\upmu\mathrm{L}}$ of $\mathrm{NH}_{2}$ -PSC $\mathrm{5~mg~mL^{-1}}$ ) was washed with ultrapure water sufficiently, whereafter $5\mathrm{mL}$ of $20\mathrm{nm}$ citrate-stabilized AuNPs solution was added.32 After 1 h of incubation at $4~^{\mathrm{{o}}}\mathrm{{C}}$ , the obtained PSC $@$ Au nanocomposites were washed three times and resuspended into $1\ \mathrm{mL}$ phosphate buffer (PBS, 0.1 M, pH 7.4). Meanwhile, DNAzyme was heated to $95~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for 5 min and slowly cooled to room temperature. For preventing disulfide formation, all thiol-modified oligonucleotides were preincubated with $10~\mathrm{mM}$ TCEP solution for $40\mathrm{min}$ . Afterwards, the mixture of $200~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ PSC@Au, $200~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ DNAzyme $(5~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ and $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ S1 $(5~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ were incubated at room temperature for $12\mathrm{{h}}$ . To maximize the loading amounts of oligonucleotides, $^{33}17\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of NaCl (1 M) was added into the above mixture solution and repeated five times at a $^{\mathrm{~1~h~}}$ interval.
After incubating at room temperature for another $24\mathrm{~h~}$ , the solution was magnetically separated to remove unconjugated oligonucleotides. Finally, the PSC@Au-DNA assembly was washed three times and then stored in $200~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ PBS (0.1 M, pH 7.4) for the following experiment.
Fabrication of the Electrochemical Biosensor. First, the glassy carbon electrode (GCE) was pretreated by alumina slurry (0.3 and $0.05~{\upmu\mathrm{m}}$ ) and then coated on a layer of AuNPs (depAu) by electrodepositing in 2 mL $\mathrm{HAuCl}_{4}$ solution $(1\%)$ at - $0.2\mathrm{~V~}$ for $30{\mathrm{~s}}.$ Then, $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ thiol-H1 $(2.0~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ was dropped onto above electrode (depAu/GCE) and incubated at room temperature for overnight. Finally, the nonspecific binding sites of modified electrode was blocked with ${}_{.0\ \upmu\mathrm{L}}$ MCH (1.0 mM) for $40\mathrm{min}$ .
Operation of Click Chemistry Reaction-Triggered 3D DNA Walking Machine.
The ligation of alkynyl-S1 with azido-S2 was performed by mixing ${8\upmu\mathrm{L}}$ azido-S2 (5 $\upmu\mathrm{M})$ , $1\upmu\mathrm{L}\ \mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ (various concentration), $1~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ AA (two-fold relative to the concentration of ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ ) and $90~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of the prepared PSC $@$ Au-alkynyl-S1, followed by incubating at room temperature for $90~\mathrm{min}$ . Afterward, the mixture was separated by magnet to remove the unconjugated azido-S2 and resuspended into $90\upmu\mathrm{L}$ PBS buffer (0.1 M, pH 7.4). Then, $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}~\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}~(10~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ was added into the above solution and incubated at $37~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $^{4\mathrm{~h~}}$ . Finally, the product DNA (S3) solution was separated by magnet for further inducing catalyzed hairpin assembly (CHA) on the electrode surface.
Experimental Measurements. Before electrochemical measurement, the modified electrode was immersed in the mixture containing $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of methylene blue-labeled
H2 (MB-H2, $2\upmu\mathrm{M}$ ) and $10~\upmu\mathrm{L}$ of the obtained S3 at $37~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for $2\textrm{h}$ to conduct CHA recycling. Afterward, the electrochemical biosensor was immersed in $2~\mathrm{mL}$ of PBS buffer (0.1 M, pH 7.4) for SWV detection from - 0.6 to $0\mathrm{~V~}$ with a frequency of 25 Hz.
Gel electrophoresis. The $16\%$ freshly prepared polyacrylamide gel was prepared with $5\times$ TBE buffer ( $445~\mathrm{mM}$ Tris, $445~\mathrm{mM}$ boric acid, $10~\mathrm{mM}$ EDTA, $\mathrm{pH}8.0\AA$ ). The electrophoresis was run at $120{\mathrm{~V~}}$ for $2.5\mathrm{~h~}$ in $1\times$ TBE buffer. After being stained by ethidium bromide (EB), the gel was imagined under UV light. Detailed reaction conditions of samples are the same as the electrochemical assay.
## RESULTS AND DISCUSSION
Polyacrylamide Gel Electrophoresis (PAGE) Characterization. The feasibility of click chemistry reaction-triggered 3D DNA walking machine operation and CHA reaction were characterized by the PAGE $(16\%)$ . As shown in Figure 1, the single bands of lane 1, 2, 5, 8 and 9 represented the individual nucleotides of S1 $(4~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ , S2 $(4~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ , hairpin-locked DNAzyme strand $(2~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ , H1 $(0.5~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ and H2 $(0.5~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ , respectively. Compared with the mixture of S1 and S2 (lane 3), the mixture of S1, S2, ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ $10~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ and AA $(20~\upmu\mathrm{M})$ generated a clear band with the higher molecular weight (lane 4), which indicated the ligation of S2 and S1. The S1 and S2 did not hybridize to DNAzyme (lane 6 vs 1, 2, and 5) for walker probe did not form. When the cofactor $\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}\left(1\upmu\mathrm{M}\right)$ was added into the mixture of DNAzyme, S1, S2, ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ and AA, a bright band with increased molecular weight and a blurry band with the fastest mobility were observed (lane 7), owing to the hybridization of walker probe with DNAzyme and the self-cleavage of DNAzyme. As a control test, the annealing reaction of H1 with H2 in the absence of products S3 was investigated by PAGE. As shown in lane 10, two bright bands corresponding to H1 and H2 and an indistinct band of H1/H2 duplex could be obviously observed. After introducing the products S3, the hybridization yield of the H1/H2 duplex (lane 11) was facilitated in contrast to that formed by the annealing of hairpin H1 and H2 (lane 10). These results demonstrated that the progression of click chemistry reaction-triggered 3D DNA walking machine could generate the S3 for further triggering CHA reaction on the electrode.
