The Effect of ${\bf{C u}}^{2+}$ and $\mathbf{M}\mathbf{g}^{2+}$ on the Analytical Performance of the Biosensor. The target ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ and cofacter $\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$ were considerable elements for click chemistry reaction-triggered 3D DNA walking machine operation, which would affect the analytical performance of the biosensor. Therefore, the proposed biosensor was investigated by SWV in the presence/absence of target ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ with/without $\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$ (Figure 4). When the biosensor was incubated with $0{\mathrm{~nM~Cu}}^{2+}$ , the alkynyl- and azido-DNA were unable to bind for the hairpin-locked DNAzyme strand opening and none of the product S3 was released, which was consistent with the result that a low SWV response was observed (curve a). In the presence of $500\ \mathrm{nM}\ \mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ but without $\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$ , the SWV response was barely changed (curve b), suggesting that the DNAzyme was not activated to cleave the self-strand for generating product S3.
When $500\ \mathrm{nM}\mathrm{Cu}^{2+}$ and $1\upmu\mathrm{M}\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$ were modified on the sensing surface, the SWV current increased dramatically (curve c). The reason might be ascribed to the fact that amounts of single strand S3 were generated by 3D DNA walking machine, resulting in the capture of many MB-DNAs onto the sensor surface with dramatically increased SWV response. Therefore, this boisensor not only realized detection of ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ , but also can be employed for $\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$ detection.
Analytical Performance of the Biosensor toward ${\bf{C u}}^{2+}$ . To investigate the analytical performance of click chemistry reaction-triggered 3D DNA walking machine, the proposed biosensor was incubated with ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ standard solution with different concentrations and performed by SWV. As shown in Figure 5A, the SWV response increased with incremental ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ concentration. Figure 5B show the SWV response was proportional to the ${\mathrm{Cu}}^{2+}$ concentration from $1.0\ \mathrm{pM}$ to $500~\mathrm{nM}$ with a regression equation expressed as $I=0.2105\mathrm{~lg~}c_{\mathrm{{Cu}}}^{\mathrm{~\tiny~2+~}}+3.286$ and the correlation coefficient was 0.9993. A detection limit of $0.33\mathrm{pM}$ for the target could be estimated. As shown in Table 1, the proposed click chemistry reaction-triggered 3D DNA walking machine strategy showed enhanced sensitivity and wider linear range compared with other reported methods, which should be attributed to the integration of the high selectivity of click chemistry reaction with the dual-amplification strategy of 3D DNA walking machine and CHA recycling. Nevertheless, this developed sensing platform consisted of 3D DNA walking machine operation and electrode assembling, which was often subjected to the complicated operation. Therefore, future development in constructing rapidness, simple and convenient sensing platform is urgently needed and should be focused.
